# Trivy ignore list (DEC-34). Every entry needs a comment, a link and an `exp:` expiry date. When an entry
# expires, Trivy reports the finding again and CI fails, so the fix can't be forgotten.

# pyasn1 0.6.4 (via pysmb): four denial-of-service bugs in ASN.1 decoding, fixed in pyasn1 0.6.5
# (https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/releases/tag/v0.6.5). 0.6.5 was uploaded on 2026-10-27 06:32 UTC, so the
# 14-day cooldown (DEC-45) admits it on 2026-11-10 at 06:33 UTC; these entries expire a day later. Then run
# `uv lock --upgrade-package pyasn1`, regenerate requirements.txt and delete these lines. Exposure until then: a
# malicious SMB server could make BECK hang or use a lot of CPU; BECK is a client the user runs by hand against
# their own Recalbox. Owner decision, 2026-11-02.
# https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-fm9c-5rcf-2q5p
CVE-2026-119194 exp:2026-11-11
